WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.869
-Guys, it is time
to announce the winner

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.038
of "The Tonight Show's
Fallon Summer Reads."

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.305
Here we go!

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:07.607
[ Band playing lively music ]

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.575
-♪ Summer Reads ♪

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.179
♪ Fallon Summer Reads ♪

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.314
-Now, here are the books
right here.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.316
Now, uh, voting has ended.

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:18.651
The polls are closed.
-That's it.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.286
-Don't even try to vote.
-Ugh.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.689
-It's over. We know
who the winner is.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.058
-You already know.
-Yeah. We already know, yeah.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:28.194
We're announcing the winner
this evening -- right now.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.329
We got hundreds
of thousands of votes.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.832
This is our biggest voting
of any year, so far.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.066
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.635
Big deal. Love that.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.670
So, thank you
to everyone who voted,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.238
and thank you
to all of our authors

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.841
for getting your enthusiasm,
getting involved in the contest,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.242
and campaigning for your books.

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.911
These are all fantastic books.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.512
They're all great.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.581
Pick them all up, if you can.
Why not? Yeah.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.450
But there can only be
one winner here.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.319
It was a close race.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.356
Yeah, just a few percentage
points separated these books.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.559
All right, I'm gonna start
breaking it down for you.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.327
[ Drum roll ]

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.762 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.331
-Oh. Oh, snap.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.901 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.102
Oh!

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.303 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:12.205
[ Goofy voice ] Boy!

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.440 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.576
Ooh! [ Stammers ]

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.612 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.415
Oh!
-"The Plot" is the book!

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.883
Congratulations!

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.920
That is this year's
"Fallon Summer Read"!

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.723
"The Plot" by
Jean Hanff Korelitz!

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.225
[ Applause ]
-Oh!

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.060
-So, here's how
this is gonna work.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.462
Once again, I have not read
any of these books.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.731
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.299
But that is how
our book club works.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:43.570
-Yeah.
-So, what I want to do
now -- this is our book.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.005
I'm gonna read this book,
and I want us all

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.206
to read it together.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.475
And then, follow us
on Instagram and Twitter

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.743
over the next few weeks.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.945
I will be checking in,
letting you know

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.214
where I'm at in the book,
what I think so far.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.616
And I want to know what you guys
think as you're reading, too.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.751 line:0%
So, use the hashtag
"#Fallon Summer Reads,"

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.153 line:0%
and we'll talk
about it together.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.620 line:0%
Thank you to everyone who voted,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.889 line:0%
and congratulations
to "The Plot"

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:05.925 line:0%
and Jean Hanff Korelitz.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.693 line:0%
We'll see you
on the show very soon.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:08.895 line:0%
Thank you, and congratulations.

